{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>An earthen vessel — it shall be broken.</b> Just as the scouring takes place in a sacred location, so the breaking requires a sacred location." "<b>In a copper vessel.</b> Scripture speaks of what is common, and the same applies to all metal vessels." "<b>And it shall be scoured and rinsed.</b> Within the time of its eating, lest one bring consecrated items to the state of נותר. One might think: just as the rinsing mentioned below is in forty se'ah, so too here in forty se'ah — therefore it writes <b>in water</b> — any amount at all."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:19.997227438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}